    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (77.96) and **Cal Raleigh** (74.07) headline our lineup, providing the highest floors for LawDog. **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** benefits from a soft matchup against Framber Valdez; his score is buoyed not just by his profile, but by the stolen base potential against a pitcher known for a slower delivery to home. Meanwhile, **Cal Raleigh** remains a priority start despite the pending lineup, as his raw power profile is maximized against Jeffrey Springs, whose 4.90 xERA suggests a high likelihood of a multi-RBI performance. **Bryce Harper** (72.70) also demands high-leverage attention; despite facing the lefty Martin P\u00e9rez, his elite xwOBA metrics allow him to transcend traditional platoon disadvantages, making him an anchor for the middle of our order.\n\nWe are aggressively deploying **Daulton Varsho** (66.94) and **Lawrence Butler** (61.72) against Brandon Pfaadt and George Kirby, respectively. **Daulton Varsho** is particularly intriguing as our primary source of stolen base efficiency today, benefiting from a favorable platoon setup. The most difficult decision this morning involved **JJ Bleday**, whose 45.87 score placed him firmly on the bubble. While **JJ Bleday** offered a respectable floor, he was ultimately edged out by the superior matchup context for **Dylan Beavers**, whose park-adjusted upside outweighed the platoon penalties affecting the rest of the bench. \n\nRisks for today center on our reliance on pending lineups for **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Zack Gelof**, **Lawrence Butler**, and **Yainer Diaz**. Specifically, **Will Smith** is staring down a difficult assignment against Cade Cavalli (3.30 xERA), and any drop in his batting order from the assumed #4 spot will compress his efficiency score rapidly. While we have depth waiting in the wings with players like **Braden Montgomery** and **Alex Freeland**, the current configuration maximizes our proximity to 5x5 production, specifically targeting speed-reliant categories where our rostered assets can outperform their raw ATC projections.",
